\subsection*{Linear overview}
The early sections match the order in which we stated our main results: \Cref{sec:pperf} deals with generalities about $p$-perfect commutative monoids and there we prove \Cref{thm:simple}; \Cref{sec:group} is about the proof of \Cref{thm:group completion} and \Cref{section:+-construction} deals with the proof of \Cref{thm:plus}. \Cref{section:module} is concerned with the comparison of $p$-perfection with another formal inversion of $p$, and there we prove \Cref{cor:agreemarc}. We added an extra section, \Cref{section: bialgebra}, which gives a different proof of a special case of \Cref{thm:plus}, because we thought the proof technique worth recording\footnote{It also happens that this proof was obtained earlier than \Cref{thm:plus}.}.

