\subsection{Summary of Main Results}

In this work, we find the scattering state and Andreev conversion probability in the lowest Landau level (LLL) for several simple nanostructures in the geometry of Fig.\,\ref{fig:Geometry}.  The nanostructures have a single gra\-phene-superconductor interface and no disorder.  
We solve the Bogoliubov-de\,Gennes (BdG) equation \cite{deGennesBook, BeenakkerRMP08, Asano_AndreevBook21} for a tight-binding model using a honeycomb lattice for graphene and a square lattice (near half filling) for the superconductor, finding the scattering state wavefunction and S-matrix.  The Andreev conversion probability as a function of the graphene chemical potential, $P_{he}(\mu_\textrm{gr})$, provides a useful way to summarize the results.  Fig.\,\ref{fig:SummaryPA} shows results for two nanostructures at four values of the graphene-superconductor interfacial coupling ($t_{NS}/t$). 

