Therefore the family of Bellman functions $\{\mbm_r\}_{r>0}$ has well-defined pointwise limits at the extremes (pictured at the opposite ends of Figure \ref{fig:acc}): as $r\rightarrow 0_+$, all but one of the triangles collapse onto the plane $\omega=0$,
    \begin{equation}
