(ii) Suppose that the nilpotent graph of $L$ is a star. Then there exists $x\in L\setminus \nil(L)$ such that $\deg(x) = |L- \nil(G)| - 1 =  |L|-|\nil(G)|-1$. Thus,  $|\nil_L(x)| = |L|$ and so $x\in \nil(L)$, which is a contradiction.
\end{proof}


