It is interesting to point out that (\ref{CDIS}) does not admit a recursion operator of the form
(\ref{RO-GEN-into}) with local symmetries $I$ and local integrating factors $\Lambda$ (see \cite{Sanders-Wang-2001}). In \cite{Niklas}
we found that (\ref{CDIS}) admits a recursion operator that generates local symmetries, and therefore a local hierarchy of equations, all of
which are linearisable under the same transformation (\ref{linearisation-CDIS}), namely the operator
\begin{gather*}
%\label{IS-hier}
%u_t=R^n[u]\,u_x, \qquad n=1,2,\ldots\ \nonumber\\[0.5cm]
