This design ensures that all cryptographic operations, including encryption, key generation, and decryption, are confined to the client side.
The blockchain layer stores only metadata and encrypted references. %, and the smart contract enforces access control policies without ever accessing raw data or keys. 
All actions, including commits, key grants, and versioning, are cryptographically signed and timestamped, offering a transparent and verifiable audit trail.

% This approach guarantees \textbf{end-to-end verifiability and confidentiality}, ensuring that only authorized users are capable of reconstructing the file, while no intermediary, including the blockchain or IPFS, has access to the plaintext content at any stage.
In this approach, IPFS stores only encrypted data file and therefore does not have access to the plaintext content at any stage. This design guarantees end to end verifiability and confidentiality, ensuring that only authorized users with the correct decryption keys can reconstruct the original file, while intermediaries including IPFS remain unable to access the plaintext data file.


