\textbf{NIC robustness evaluation}. The primary application of our framework is to systematically evaluate the resilience of learning-based codecs to different adversarial attacks. NIC-RobustBench implements the entire evaluation pipeline, from the generation of adversarial examples and evaluation of NIC model on clear and malicious data to the processing of the results. Figure \ref{fig:results}~(a) presents the Rate-Distortion curves (SSIM/BPP) obtained with our framework for both source (dashed lines) and attacked (solid lines) images. Subfigures demonstrate two optimization targets for the attacks, with left targeting the compression quality, and bitrate on the right. One can immediately notice the significant shift in RD performance in the adversarial scenario for all tested NIC models, emphasizing their vulnerability. Figure \ref{fig:results}~(b, left) numerically evaluates this gap in compression quality with $\Delta_{score}$ based on VMAF metric. MBT-2018, Balle et al. and Cheng et al. (only the attention-based variation) models demonstrate the best robustness in this test. Interestingly, generative-compression models (diffusion-based CDC, GAN-based HiFiC, QRes-VAE) are among the least stable.
