\end{figure}
\cref{fig:alpha-example-L3} shows the result of the alpha miner for the event log $L_3$, containing isolated nodes.
Due to this behavior of the alpha algorithm, we can find counter-examples showing that none of the log complexity measures can predict the model complexity of the alpha algorithm's output.
The only exception is the number of duplicate tasks $\duplicate$, which is always $0$, since we create exactly one transition for each distinct activity in the event log.
\cref{table:alphaminer-findings} shows our findings.

